description:
Implement `createReactive(obj)` which returns a Proxy that tracks property reads and writes, and `computed(fn)` which returns a lazily-evaluated value that automatically re-runs `fn` when its reactive dependencies change.

The computed object has a `.value` getter that returns the current result, and re-evaluates only when dependencies have changed.

**Example:**
```js
const state = createReactive({ count: 1 });
const doubled = computed(() => state.count * 2);
console.log(doubled.value); // 2
state.count = 5;
console.log(doubled.value); // 10
```

